<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows $101.4 mln June 12.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows $101.4 mln June 12.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $101.4 million deficit on June 12 in the commercial forex market, according to the Central Bank.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 12</p>
<p>Exports: $229.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $312.3 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $232.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $251 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $101.4 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UPDATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.035 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.394 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.471 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.166 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $54 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
